 "title": "Two layers enforce the rules",
 "desc": "An isometric scene in two parts with a wall between them. On the left, the AI's session in Claude Code: hooks and permission rules refuse an edit of a locked file, a push, and a merge. At the wall, git runs pre-commit on each commit, merge, and push. On the right, the main branch and the signed records: a merge into main needs a signed pass record, and a risky change also needs your signed approval. A commit goes in on one lane; a refusal comes back on the other. Behind both layers, the gate and the signed records hold even when a layer is skipped.",
